# SIH 2026 — PS ID 26103
## AI-Powered Predictive Analytics & Early Warning System for Infrastructure Project Monitoring
### Complete Solution Architecture & Implementation Roadmap
**Organization:** Ministry of Statistics & Programme Implementation (MoSPI) | **Data Source:** PAIMANA / OCMS Flash Reports

---

## 0. Executive Summary

The system ingests 14 monthly PAIMANA Flash Report PDFs (₹150 Cr+ projects, ~1,700–2,000 projects/month, 17 Ministries, 22 sectors), converts them into a **longitudinal (panel) time-series master dataset** keyed by Project ID × Report Month, engineers delay/overrun features, trains ML models to predict **cost overrun risk**, **time delay risk**, and an aggregate **Project Risk Score**, and exposes this through a **FastAPI backend + React dashboard** with **explainable AI** (SHAP) so MoSPI officials can see *why* a project is flagged and *what to do about it*.

**Core design principle:** Treat each project as a **time-series entity**, not a static row. The same Project ID recurs across 14 reports — this repeated measurement is the single richest signal in the dataset (trend of cost creep, progress velocity, stagnation streaks) and must drive the feature engineering strategy.

