### **Phase 6 — ML Model Selection & Comparison**

**Objective:** Select the best-performing, most explainable models per target.

**Candidate Models (in order of recommended trial):**

| Task | Baseline | Primary Candidates | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cost Overrun Risk (classification) | Logistic Regression | **XGBoost / LightGBM**, Random Forest | Gradient boosting handles mixed types, outliers, non-linearity well; strong SHAP support |
| Time Delay Risk (classification) | Logistic Regression | **LightGBM**, CatBoost (good native categorical handling for Ministry/Sector/State) | |
| Composite Risk Score (regression) | Linear Regression | **XGBoost Regressor**, Gradient Boosting Regressor | |
| Sequence-aware alternative (stretch goal) | — | LSTM / GRU on the panel sequence, or Temporal Fusion Transformer | Only if time permits — needs more data per project (14 points is short for deep sequence models); tree models on engineered trend features are the pragmatic SIH-timeline choice |

**Processing Steps:**
1. Time-based train/validation/test split (train on early months, validate/test on later months) — mimics real deployment where you predict the future.
2. Handle class imbalance (overrun/delay classes likely imbalanced) via `class_weight='balanced'`, or SMOTE/ADASYN on training fold only.
3. Hyperparameter tuning via `Optuna` with time-series-aware cross-validation (`sklearn.model_selection.TimeSeriesSplit` adapted to project-panel structure — group by `project_uid` to avoid leaking the same project across folds).
4. Evaluate with metrics appropriate to imbalanced classification: F1 (macro), ROC-AUC, PR-AUC, confusion matrix per class; regression: RMSE, MAE, R².
5. Compare models on a leaderboard; log every run to MLflow.
6. Select final model(s) balancing accuracy vs. interpretability (favor LightGBM/XGBoost — strong accuracy + native SHAP compatibility, critical for the Explainable AI requirement).

**Outputs:** Trained model artifacts, MLflow experiment log, model comparison report.

**Deliverables:** `best_model_cost.pkl`, `best_model_delay.pkl`, `best_model_riskscore.pkl`, comparison report.

**Recommended Tools:** `scikit-learn`, `XGBoost`, `LightGBM`, `CatBoost`, `Optuna`, `MLflow`, `imbalanced-learn`.

